 of  ahsoka tano and he always had a  particular iron toward librarian jocasta  nu who had denied him access to the jedi  archives we actually meet this grand  inquisitor in season one of rebels  voiced by jason isaacs when he used the  corpse of the jedi luminar unduly to  lure kanan and ezra into a trap now by  the end of that season kanan's able to  defeat the grand inquisitor allowing  himself to fall to his death you have no  idea what you've unleashed here today  there are some things far more  frightening than death  but now the grand inquisitor's deeper  relationship with vader is being  explored in this series and the rivalry  between these two is a delight it was  actually first shown in the 2017 comics  when palpatine allowed these two to  clash without even telling them that  they were on the same side without even  telling vader that the inquisitors even  existed this is back when the  inquisitors were being trained out of a  headquarters based on coruscant called  the works before relocating to the ocean  world of nur where they are in the  obi-wan kenobi series now when vader and  the grand inquisitor first clashed both  of these servants of the emperor thought  that they and only they were the  emperor's number one and that first  impression left the two with a bitter  rivalry honestly if there's anything  this creepy old man loves it's two boys  who both thought they were his favorite  locking sabers as he looks for a window  to sneer do it he loves to sit and watch  so at this point vader is given command  of the inquisitors to teach them in his  ways of cruelty he does this by being  cruel severing their limbs to teach them  the lesson of loss because if our  generation had to learn by getting our  bodies burned to hell on a hot stove  it's how the younger generation must  also learn it now during these early  years joe costa new sneaks back into the  jedi temple to retrieve a hologram  containing a list of force sensitive  kids but like any great librarian she  cannot help or reprimand some snotty  little kid who she said no to so she  jumps down engages the grand inquisitor  in the two fight but vader intervenes  and despite being told by the emperor to  return jocasta to him alive along with  her holocron vader kills jocasta and  crushes the holocron showing how this  guy actually does not want to make  friends he doesn't want the emperor to  make more sid he doesn't want to work  with the inquisitors he wants to work  alone which gives us a bit of context to  how vader now is in this series so along  with the grand inquisitor let's quickly  remind ourselves of the other identified  inquisitors in star wars canon so on  this obi-wan kenobi series we have the  third sister riva whom we're still  getting to know we also have the fifth  brother now the fifth brother along with  the seventh sister will later have huge  roles in season two of rebels  confronting kanan and ezra on malachor  and that arc also shows us the eighth  brother who's an inquisitor tasking with  hunting down maul but when all of these  hunters and fugitives end up in a melee  the inquisitors don't make it out alive  now this series also introduces us to  the fourth sister interesting that we're  now seeing this inquisitor because in  the 2019 return to vader's castle comics  by kevin scott we learned the fourth  sister's armor ends up in the hands of  rebel commander lena graff who used this  armor as a disguise to infiltrate  vader's mustafar castle and free her  lieutenant hud so something's gonna go  down with this fourth sister and that  rebel commander now those 2017 comics  also show us the sixth brother bill  valen who first appeared in the 2016  ahsoka novel by ek johnston the sixth  brother confronted ahsoka on the planet  radha and ahsoka extracted the kyber  crystals from his spinning blade causing  his saber to explode in his face and  kill him and leaving her with those two  white blades that she wields in rebels  and in the mandalorian season two the  2017 comics also first show us the ninth  sister later revealed to have the name  of masana tide a major character in the  game jedi fallen order who ends up  defeated by calcus on kashyyyk falling  out of a high tree nest but her fate  unknown really the main antagonist of  jedi fallen order is the second sister  trilla sugary padawan to seared junda  the game actually allows you to explore  the fortress inquisitorius on ner and  it's here where trailer fails to kill  calcus and for that failure darth vader  executes her another known inquisitor is  the tenth brother prosset dibs who is a  jedi master who previously tried to kill  mace windu and was imprisoned but after  order 66 the tables turn and he is  recruited to join the inquisitorius in  the 2017 run he joins vader and other  inquisitors on a mission to mancala  where they engage the escaped jedi  fugitive pharyn barr who manipulated  some purge strippers to fire a  pon-prosset and kill him and then a few  issues after this we meet two other  inquisitors a male twee-like inquisitor  and a female [ __ ] inquisitor who end  up kidnapping the infant daughter of the  escaped jedi eve coth and afterwards  when they celebrate vader's senses of  camaraderie between these two views it  as weak and phrases the two of them with  the force so they each die on each  other's sabers there has been another  inquisitor over the years who's been  mentioned jurcera who's a deathmarian  who was trained by some unknown female  inquisitor until jacera killed that  master and took her lightsaber but what  is most intriguing about the inquisitor  numbering system is even though we've  only met a scattered disorder few of  them there presumably are other brothers  and sisters filling in that roster maybe  lucasfilm will fill it all in maybe  leave some of the ranks forever a  mystery but with every inquisitor we  meet it is clear that they were brought  up to embrace their inner hatred their  rage the